======================================================================================================================
PART A -- THE ADJUDICATION.  What does the framework's own derivation give?
======================================================================================================================
  H_Lambda = H0 sqrt(OL) = 1.80824e-18 1/s;  L_dS = sqrt(3/Lambda) = c/H_Lambda = 5373.0 Mpc
  a0 = c^2/(2 pi L_dS)            = 8.62775e-11 m/s^2   (the brief's form; = c H_Lambda/2pi)
  a0 = (c/2) sqrt(G rho_DE)       = 9.36457e-11 m/s^2   (kappa = 1/2, the CANONICAL footing)
  a0 = c H_Lambda / Z             = 9.36457e-11 m/s^2   (identical to the line above)
  a0 = c H0 / Z  (rho = rho_tot today) = 1.13053e-10 m/s^2   (the ALT footing)
  [PASS] A-1  the two forms of the CANONICAL footing are the same number: (c/2)sqrt(G rho_DE) = c H_Lambda/Z, and it reproduces the committed canonical a0 to 1%   ((c/2)sqrt(G rho_DE) = 9.36457e-11 = c H_L/Z = 9.36457e-11;  committed 9.3619e-11 (ratio 1.0003))
  [PASS] A-2  the brief's a0 = c^2/(2 pi L_dS) is NOT the framework's canonical footing: it is Z/(2pi) = 0.921 of it (8% low).  The framework's kappa = 1/2 is a DIFFERENT posit from the naive de Sitter-Unruh 1/2pi -- stated so no number here is quietly swapped for the other   (a0(2pi form)/a0(canonical) = 0.9213 = Z/2pi;  a0(2pi form) = 8.6277e-11 m/s^2)
  [PASS] A-3  a0/(c H0): the scale IS a dark-energy-scale acceleration, order 1/2pi -- the framework's signature   (canonical 0.1431, alt 0.1723, 1/2pi = 0.1592)
  [PASS] A-4  THE FORK IS LITERALLY 'WHICH rho': (c/2)sqrt(G rho_crit(z)) = c H(z)/Z identically, so branch B is branch A's own formula with rho_DE -> rho_tot(z).  Nothing else distinguishes them   ((c/2)sqrt(G rho_tot(z)) == c H(z)/Z to machine precision)
  [PASS] A-5  THE TWO COMMITTED FOOTINGS ARE THE FORK EVALUATED TODAY: alt/canonical = 1/sqrt(OL). The repository's 'both footings' habit already carries branch A and branch B at z = 0; they only diverge backwards   (alt/canonical = 1.2048  vs  1/sqrt(OL) = 1.2072)
  
  ADJUDICATION.  The derivation reads the scale off the DE SITTER HORIZON: L_dS = sqrt(3/Lambda), and
  Lambda is a constant of the action.  Every route the programme certifies (MacDowell-Mansouri SO(4,1),
  the de Sitter-Unruh quadrature, the conformal-SO(4,1) and gauge-Yang-Mills routes) forces the FORM
  a0 propto c^2 sqrt(Lambda) -- i.e. rho = rho_DE.  None of them contains rho_matter or rho_radiation.
  => BRANCH A is what the derivation implies.  With w = -1 exactly, a0 is a CONSTANT for all time.
  BRANCH B (a0 propto H) requires replacing rho_DE by rho_tot -- a different posit, not the derivation,
  and the repository's own papers label it 'the rival rising branch'.
  LCDM's own emergent halo acceleration scale: naive g_dagger ~ sqrt(G rho_crit(z)) gives EXACTLY E(z), i.e. branch B's law; the full halo-structure law E^(4/3) c^2/f(c) gives +0.327 dex at z = 2.5 vs branch B's +0.575
  [PASS] A-6  BRANCH B IS NOT A DISTINCTIVE PREDICTION -- but the statement must be made precisely.  Its law a0 propto H(z) is IDENTICALLY the naive LCDM expectation for the emergent halo scale, g_dagger ~ sqrt(G rho_crit(z)) propto H(z), so the LEADING scaling is shared with a dark-matter halo population and carries no distinctive content.  The two are NOT numerically identical: the full halo-structure law differs by 0.249 dex at z = 2.5.  It is branch A (FLAT) that is the distinctive one, because LCDM has no way to make the scale constant   (sqrt(G rho_crit(z)) = E(z) sqrt(G rho_crit(0)) identically; but LCDM halo law +0.327 dex vs branch B +0.575 dex at z = 2.5 (differ by 0.249 dex))

